  "term": "neurofibrillary tangles",
  "definition": "Neurofibrillary tangles are abnormal clumps inside brain cells made of tightly packed twisted filaments involving neurofilaments, microtubule-related proteins, actin, and ubiquitins. They are a major biological feature of Alzheimer disease and, after death, higher numbers of tangles are associated with more severe dementia during life.",
